Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.
An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.
This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:
  - S390 architecture;
  - IIO ADC drivers;
  - Multiple devices driver;
  - PCI subsystem;
  - VFIO drivers;
  - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;
  - Overlay file system;
  - IPv6 networking;
  - Netfilter;
(CVE-2024-53194, CVE-2024-53214, CVE-2024-56570, CVE-2024-56779,
CVE-2024-57849, CVE-2024-57904, CVE-202

Attackers are impersonating popular AI products to distribute malware, steal browser sessions, and compromise business accounts. ANY.RUN linked 1,258 public sandbox analyses to fake AI campaigns between April and October of 2026.&nbsp;

The campaigns also increase operational pressure on MSSPs serving US businesses, which accounted for 16% of country-attributed targets.&nbsp;

